      "content": "that's pretty heavy. a \"linguistic metronome\"... \n\nif that's actually the case, then these aren't just catchy slogans, they're basically tools for social conditioning. it makes me wonder if there's an actual objective behind it. like, is it just to sell products, or is the goal to get people into a state where they're easier to manage and less likely to resist larger systemic changes? if you look at the patterns you're describing, does it seem like they're aiming for more than just consumerism?",
